<!DOCTYPE html><html  lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Telegram integration for AI agents and workflows | StackOS</title><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_54a4nl.png"><meta name="twitter:image:src" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_54a4nl.png"><meta property="og:image" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_54a4nl.png"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta name="twitter:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="600"><meta name="twitter:image:height" content="600"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/entry.z7ALz4wj.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/_slug_.CMebKqZb.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/useIntegrationCatalog.wtjwSlpy.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/integrationRoutePolicy.BHfEqrhY.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/LibraryFrame.CD2pOTex.css" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/fonts/manrope-latin-variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous"><link rel="preload" as="fetch" crossorigin="anonymous" href="/library/integrations/telegram/_payload.json?aa8e47a4-cf64-43ed-8aa2-6473b185d6eb"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/BT73oLzS.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/BlBH4eXS.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/D6cldFGh.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/ik2kKGEl.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/CBNv9QJs.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/Dbua9CwJ.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/DIYlYVLR.js"><script type="module" src="/_nuxt/BT73oLzS.js" crossorigin></script><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/stackos-icon.png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/images/stackos-icon.png"><link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="StackOS Library" href="/feed.xml"><meta name="description" content="Telegram bot and user Accounts with one managed TDLib session per Account. Explore 17 listed Telegram actions and see how it fits into StackOS workflows."><meta name="theme-color" content="#090b10"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="Telegram integration for AI agents and workflows | StackOS"><meta property="og:description" content="Telegram bot and user Accounts with one managed TDLib session per Account. Explore 17 listed Telegram actions and see how it fits into StackOS workflows."><meta name="twitter:title" content="Telegram integration for AI agents and workflows | StackOS"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Telegram bot and user Accounts with one managed TDLib session per Account. Explore 17 listed Telegram actions and see how it fits into StackOS workflows."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1"><link rel="canonical" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/telegram/"><meta property="og:url" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/telegram/"><script type="application/ld+json" data-hid="integration-software">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Telegram","description":"Telegram bot and user Accounts with one managed TDLib session per Account.","applicationCategory":"Communications","url":"https://telegram.org/"}</script><script type="application/ld+json" data-hid="integration-faq">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What can the Telegram integration do in StackOS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The current catalog includes 17 Telegram actions across Messaging. The exact actions used depend on the workflow and approval rules."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does StackOS replace Telegram?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Telegram remains the tool that performs its part of the job. StackOS organizes the workflow, keeps status and dependencies visible, and calls the tool only when the plan reaches the right approved action."}}]}</script><meta property="og:site_name" content="StackOS"><script id="unhead:payload" type="application/json">{"titleTemplate":"%s | StackOS"}</script></head><body><div id="__nuxt"><!--[--><div id="top" class="site library-site" data-v-76ae88b3 data-v-e230b581><a class="skip-link" href="#main" data-v-e230b581>Skip to content</a><header class="site-header" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell site-header__inner"><a href="/" class="brand" aria-label="StackOS home"><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width="36" height="36"><span>StackOS</span><small>Work, organized</small></a><nav class="site-nav site-nav--desktop" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav><details class="mobile-menu"><summary role="button" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-controls="site-navigation"><span></span><span></span></summary><nav id="site-navigation" class="site-nav site-nav--mobile" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav></details></div></header><div class="library-nav" aria-label="Library sections" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell library-nav__inner" data-v-e230b581><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Workflows</a><a href="/library/agents/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Agents</a><a href="/library/orchestrators/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Orchestrators</a><a href="/library/integrations/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Integrations</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Articles</a></div></div><main id="main" class="library-main" data-v-e230b581><nav class="library-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-v-e230b581 data-v-59391fa3><div class="shell" data-v-59391fa3><ol data-v-59391fa3><!--[--><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Home</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Library</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/integrations/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Integrations</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a aria-current="page" href="/library/integrations/telegram/" class="router-link-active router-link-exact-active" data-v-59391fa3>Telegram</a></li><!--]--></ol></div></nav><!--[--><section class="integration-detail-hero" style="--integration-color:#7ee2ad;" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="shell integration-detail-hero__grid" data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><div class="integration-detail-hero__identity" data-v-76ae88b3><span class="integration-mark is-large has-logo" style="--mark-color:#7ee2ad;" aria-hidden="true" data-v-76ae88b3 data-v-aa7c01f7><img src="/images/integrations/telegram.png" alt="" data-v-aa7c01f7></span><div data-v-76ae88b3><a href="/library/integrations/plugins/communications/" class="" data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Communications plugin</span></a><h1 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram</h1></div></div><p data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram bot and user Accounts with one managed TDLib session per Account.</p><div class="integration-detail-hero__meta" data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3><strong data-v-76ae88b3>17</strong> listed actions</span><span data-v-76ae88b3><strong data-v-76ae88b3>1</strong> capability groups</span></div></div><aside data-v-76ae88b3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Use Telegram inside a complete plan.</p><strong data-v-76ae88b3>StackOS keeps the request, status, approvals, and proof connected around every tool action.</strong><div data-v-76ae88b3><!--[--><a href="https://telegram.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-76ae88b3>Visit tool <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-76ae88b3>↗</span></a><a href="https://core.telegram.org/tdlib" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-76ae88b3>Documentation <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-76ae88b3>↗</span></a><a href="https://telegram.org/apps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-76ae88b3>Create account <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-76ae88b3>↗</span></a><a href="https://my.telegram.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-76ae88b3>Open console <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-76ae88b3>↗</span></a><!--]--></div></aside></div></section><section class="integration-facts" data-provider-facts="telegram" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="shell" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="library-section__heading" data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><p class="eyebrow" data-v-76ae88b3>Connection facts</p><h2 data-v-76ae88b3>What the Telegram connector actually exposes.</h2></div><p data-v-76ae88b3>These details come from the current StackOS provider manifest and action catalog. They describe the available connection—not a promise that every workflow will use every action.</p></div><dl class="integration-facts__grid" data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><dt data-v-76ae88b3>Connection method</dt><dd data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram application credentials and bot token or user sign-in</dd></div><div data-v-76ae88b3><dt data-v-76ae88b3>Setup</dt><dd data-v-76ae88b3>Register a Telegram application at my.telegram.org/apps for a shared API ID and hash once. Each bot also needs its own token from BotFather. For a user, complete Telegram&#39;s authorization challenge in Account setup. Configure an optional SOCKS5, HTTP, or MTProto proxy on the same Account. To correct the shared application pair, detach and revoke every Telegram Account; revoking the final Account resets the application setting for the next setup.</dd></div><div data-v-76ae88b3><dt data-v-76ae88b3>Capability groups</dt><dd data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</dd></div><div data-v-76ae88b3><dt data-v-76ae88b3>Action boundaries</dt><dd data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>8 read actions</span><span data-v-76ae88b3>9 write actions</span><!----><!----><!----></dd></div></dl></div></section><!----><!----><section class="integration-actions" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="shell" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="library-section__heading" data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><p class="eyebrow" data-v-76ae88b3>Action catalog</p><h2 data-v-76ae88b3>Actions listed for Telegram.</h2></div><p data-v-76ae88b3>Actions listed for this integration. Individual descriptions note availability limits. A workflow still decides which actions belong in the job and where approval is required.</p></div><div class="integration-action-tools" data-v-76ae88b3><label for="action-query" data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Search Telegram actions</span><input id="action-query" value="" type="search" placeholder="Search 17 actions…" autocomplete="off" data-v-76ae88b3></label><!----><p data-v-76ae88b3>17 matching actions</p></div><div class="integration-action-grid" data-v-76ae88b3><!--[--><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Album Send</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib album send for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Callback Answer</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib callback answer for a bot Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-read" data-v-76ae88b3>Reads data</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Chat Inspect</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib chat inspect for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile. Returns bounded chat and membership facts. Use action.run with response_mode=raw and no idempotency key for this transient read.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-read" data-v-76ae88b3>Reads data</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Chat List</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Read one bounded page of a connected user Account&#39;s Main or Archive chats from TDLib. The cursor slices TDLib&#39;s current ordered list; chat reordering can shift pages. No chat messages are stored by this action. Use action.run with response_mode=raw and no idempotency key to receive this transient page.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-read" data-v-76ae88b3>Reads data</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Chat Resolve</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib chat resolve for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile. Returns a bounded chat summary. Use action.run with response_mode=raw and no idempotency key for this transient read.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-read" data-v-76ae88b3>Reads data</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Chat Sender List</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Read the selected and available TDLib sender identities for one chat through a connected bot or user Account. Use a returned sender_ref on a later explicit send when choosing to post as a channel. Use action.run with response_mode=raw and no idempotency key for this transient read.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-read" data-v-76ae88b3>Reads data</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram File Download</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib file download for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-read" data-v-76ae88b3>Reads data</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Identity Get</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib identity get for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Message Broadcast</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib message broadcast for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Message Delete</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib message delete for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Message Edit</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib message edit for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Message Forward</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib message forward for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-read" data-v-76ae88b3>Reads data</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Message Get</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib message get for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile. Returns selected text and account-qualified file refs without the full native message object. Use action.run with response_mode=raw and no idempotency key for this transient read.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-read" data-v-76ae88b3>Reads data</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Message History</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Read one bounded, newest-first TDLib history page from a known user Account chat. Pass next_before_message_id as before_message_id for the next page; a short page is not proof of the end. Full text requires include_content. No fetched messages are stored as communication resources by this action. Use action.run with response_mode=raw and no idempotency key to receive this transient page.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Message React</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib message react for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Message Send</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib message send for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><article data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><span data-v-76ae88b3>Messaging</span><b class="is-write" data-v-76ae88b3>Can make changes</b></div><h3 data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram Poll Stop</h3><p data-v-76ae88b3>Explicit TDLib poll stop for a bot or user Account through its project communication profile.</p></article><!--]--></div><!----></div></section><section class="integration-answer" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="detail-body__narrow" data-v-76ae88b3><p class="eyebrow" data-v-76ae88b3>Direct answer</p><h2 data-v-76ae88b3>How does the Telegram integration work?</h2><p data-v-76ae88b3>People continue using Telegram as their tool. StackOS adds it to a visible workflow, keeps the work in order, and passes only the approved action to the integration when that stage is ready.</p><ol class="integration-route-flow" style="--route-color:#7ee2ad;" data-integration-route="telegram" aria-label="How StackOS routes approved work to Telegram" data-v-76ae88b3 data-v-4eb1f27f><!--[--><li data-v-4eb1f27f><span data-v-4eb1f27f>01</span><strong data-v-4eb1f27f>Your request</strong><small data-v-4eb1f27f>Start in your AI</small></li><li data-v-4eb1f27f><span data-v-4eb1f27f>02</span><strong data-v-4eb1f27f>StackOS plan</strong><small data-v-4eb1f27f>Expands the steps</small></li><li data-v-4eb1f27f><span data-v-4eb1f27f>03</span><strong data-v-4eb1f27f>Telegram</strong><small data-v-4eb1f27f>Does its bounded part</small></li><li data-v-4eb1f27f><span data-v-4eb1f27f>04</span><strong data-v-4eb1f27f>Checked result</strong><small data-v-4eb1f27f>Keeps the proof</small></li><!--]--></ol></div></section><section class="related-section" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="shell" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="library-section__heading" data-v-76ae88b3><div data-v-76ae88b3><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark" data-v-76ae88b3>More from Communications</p><h2 data-v-76ae88b3>Related integrations.</h2></div><a href="/library/integrations/plugins/communications/" class="" data-v-76ae88b3>See the plugin →</a></div><div class="integration-related-grid" data-v-76ae88b3><!--[--><article class="integration-card" style="--integration-color:#7ee2ad;" data-v-76ae88b3 data-v-480388d2><div class="integration-card__top" data-v-480388d2><span class="integration-mark is-small has-logo is-wordmark is-dark-logo" style="--mark-color:#7ee2ad;" aria-hidden="true" data-v-480388d2 data-v-aa7c01f7><img src="/images/integrations/imap.svg" alt="" data-v-aa7c01f7></span><span data-v-480388d2>Communications</span></div><a href="/library/integrations/imap/" class="integration-card__body" data-v-480388d2><h2 data-v-480388d2>IMAP</h2><p data-v-480388d2>IMAP provider for mailbox listing, search, metadata fetch, bounded evidence staging, and message flag lifecycle.</p></a><div class="integration-card__capabilities" data-v-480388d2><!--[--><span data-v-480388d2>Email Inbox</span><!--]--><!----></div><footer data-v-480388d2><a href="/library/integrations/imap/" class="" data-v-480388d2>7 actions <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-480388d2>→</span></a><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9051.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-480388d2> Visit tool <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-480388d2>↗</span></a></footer></article><article class="integration-card" style="--integration-color:#7ee2ad;" data-v-76ae88b3 data-v-480388d2><div class="integration-card__top" data-v-480388d2><span class="integration-mark is-small has-logo" style="--mark-color:#7ee2ad;" aria-hidden="true" data-v-480388d2 data-v-aa7c01f7><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" data-v-aa7c01f7></span><span data-v-480388d2>Communications</span></div><a href="/library/integrations/local-agent-chat/" class="integration-card__body" data-v-480388d2><h2 data-v-480388d2>Local Agent Chat</h2><p data-v-480388d2>StackOS local conversation surface for direct human-to-agent messages, rich response blocks, and interaction events.</p></a><div class="integration-card__capabilities" data-v-480388d2><!--[--><!--]--><!----></div><footer data-v-480388d2><a href="/library/integrations/local-agent-chat/" class="" data-v-480388d2>Learn more <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-480388d2>→</span></a><!----></footer></article><article class="integration-card" style="--integration-color:#7ee2ad;" data-v-76ae88b3 data-v-480388d2><div class="integration-card__top" data-v-480388d2><span class="integration-mark is-small has-logo" style="--mark-color:#7ee2ad;" aria-hidden="true" data-v-480388d2 data-v-aa7c01f7><img src="/images/integrations/slack-icon.png" alt="" data-v-aa7c01f7></span><span data-v-480388d2>Communications</span></div><a href="/library/integrations/slack-bot/" class="integration-card__body" data-v-480388d2><h2 data-v-480388d2>Slack Bot</h2><p data-v-480388d2>Slack Web API provider for bot identity, message sends, conversation discovery, membership sync, and signed HTTP ingress.</p></a><div class="integration-card__capabilities" data-v-480388d2><!--[--><span data-v-480388d2>Messaging</span><!--]--><!----></div><footer data-v-480388d2><a href="/library/integrations/slack-bot/" class="" data-v-480388d2>10 actions <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-480388d2>→</span></a><a href="https://slack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-480388d2> Visit tool <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-480388d2>↗</span></a></footer></article><!--]--></div></div></section><section class="integration-faq" aria-labelledby="integration-faq-title" data-v-76ae88b3><div class="detail-body__narrow" data-v-76ae88b3><p class="eyebrow" data-v-76ae88b3>Common questions</p><h2 id="integration-faq-title" data-v-76ae88b3>Telegram and StackOS.</h2><!--[--><details data-v-76ae88b3><summary data-v-76ae88b3>What can the Telegram integration do in StackOS?</summary><p data-v-76ae88b3>The current catalog includes 17 Telegram actions across Messaging. The exact actions used depend on the workflow and approval rules.</p></details><details data-v-76ae88b3><summary data-v-76ae88b3>Does StackOS replace Telegram?</summary><p data-v-76ae88b3>No. Telegram remains the tool that performs its part of the job. StackOS organizes the workflow, keeps status and dependencies visible, and calls the tool only when the plan reaches the right approved action.</p></details><!--]--></div></section><!--]--></main><footer class="site-footer" data-v-e230b581 data-v-5f58f905><div class="shell site-footer__grid" data-v-5f58f905><a href="/" class="footer-brand" data-v-5f58f905><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-5f58f905><div data-v-5f58f905><strong data-v-5f58f905>StackOS</strong><span data-v-5f58f905>Keep AI-powered work clear, connected, and moving.</span></div></a><div class="site-footer__links" data-v-5f58f905><div data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>Explore</span><a href="/#why" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Why StackOS</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Getting started</a><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Workflows</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Articles</a></div><div data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>Build</span><a href="/#security" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Security</a><a href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac" data-v-5f58f905>Download</a><a href="https://github.com/flowmonkeyio/StackOS" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-v-5f58f905>GitHub ↗</a></div></div><div class="site-footer__status" data-v-5f58f905><span class="status-dot" data-v-5f58f905></span><div data-v-5f58f905><strong data-v-5f58f905>Runs on your Mac</strong><small data-v-5f58f905>Your work. Your apps. Your private logins.</small></div></div></div><div class="shell site-footer__bottom" data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>StackOS · You